Create an issue with labels, priority and a Markdown description, then read it back.

live: true
-- file desc.md --
## Steps

1. Open `linear`
2. 中文 + emoji ✅
-- run --
linear issue create --team {{TEAM}} --title "{{RUN}} create: hello+world" --label Bug --label Feature --priority high --description-file desc.md --json
-- stdout.json --
{
  "ok": true,
  "effect": "applied",
  "data": {
    "success": true,
    "issue": {
      "id": "{{=ISSUE_ID}}",
      "identifier": "{{=ISSUE}}",
      "title": "{{RUN}} create: hello+world",
      "url": "https://linear.app/kadoraba/issue/{{ISSUE}}/{{RUN}}-create-helloworld",
      "team": { "key": "ENG" },
      "state": { "id": "{{*}}", "name": "Backlog", "type": "backlog" },
      "assignee": null,
      "project": null,
      "parent": null,
      "labels": {
        "nodes": [
          { "id": "{{*}}", "name": "Bug" },
          { "id": "{{*}}", "name": "Feature" }
        ],
        "pageInfo": { "hasNextPage": false, "endCursor": "{{*}}" }
      }
    }
  },
  "fields": [
    { "inputField": "title", "field": "title", "desired": "{{RUN}} create: hello+world", "verdict": "write" },
    { "inputField": "priority", "field": "priority", "desired": 2, "verdict": "write" },
    { "inputField": "labelIds", "field": "labels", "desired": ["{{*}}", "{{*}}"], "verdict": "write" },
    { "inputField": "teamId", "field": "team", "desired": "{{*}}", "verdict": "write" },
    { "inputField": "description", "field": "description", "desired": "## Steps\n\n1. Open `linear`\n2. 中文 + emoji ✅\n", "verdict": "write" }
  ]
}
-- stderr --
{{ISSUE}} has no --project or --parent. Decide ownership from the candidate Project's full content and the related Initiative content (linear guide issue-authoring), then save the original read and set the project: (if [ -e original.json ] || [ -L original.json ]; then echo 'original.json exists' >&2; exit 1; fi; t=$(mktemp original.json.XXXXXX) || exit; s=0; linear issue view '{{ISSUE}}' --json >| "$t" || { cat "$t" >&2; s=1; }; [ "$s" != 0 ] || ln "$t" original.json || s=1; rm -f "$t"; exit "$s") && linear issue update '{{ISSUE}}' --project <project> --base-file original.json
